{"id":2611,"date":"2023-08-21T19:51:00","date_gmt":"2023-08-21T18:51:00","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/?p=2611"},"modified":"2024-02-15T09:30:08","modified_gmt":"2024-02-15T09:30:08","slug":"ccac-co-designer-aurelie-fontan-wins-young-innovators-next-steps-award","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/ccac-co-designer-aurelie-fontan-wins-young-innovators-next-steps-award\/","title":{"rendered":"CCAC 2022 Co-designer at Ordsall Primary School wins a Young Innovators Next Steps Award"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text alignwide has-media-on-the-right is-stacked-on-mobile is-vertically-aligned-top\"><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Amazingly <a href=\"https:\/\/www.aureliefontan.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Aur\u00e9lie Fontan<\/a>, a pioneer CCAC co-design collaborator and winner in the <a href=\"https:\/\/www.arts.ac.uk\/colleges\/london-college-of-fashion\/stories\/pangaia-and-fashion-district-announce-winner-of-design-futures-innovation-prize\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">UAL competition, Design Futures, sponsored by PANGAIA<\/a> has won a further major financial award, <a href=\"https:\/\/iuk.ktn-uk.org\/programme\/young-innovators\/next-steps\/\">The Young Innovators Next Steps Awards<\/a>.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The win represents another milestone for Aur\u00e9lie, her co-founder Meredith Wood, and her symbiotic fashion brand <a href=\"https:\/\/www.osmosestudio.co.uk\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">OSMOSE<\/a>. &nbsp;OSMOSE works to reshape and replace the environmentally damaging synthetic dyes and colour systems used in the fashion industry, while looking to remedy the UK ecosystem by replenishing soil health and supporting regenerative agriculture.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The concept is now at Technology Readiness Level (TRL) 3. With the Award, Aurelie plans to work with scientists to develop her idea and move up to TRL5, before taking it to the wider market in the UK and EU.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You can read more about Aur\u00e9lie and her co-design work at Ordsall School <a href=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/fashioning-a-better-future-at-ordsall-primary-school\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">here<\/a><\/p>\n<\/div><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"664\" height=\"1000\" data-src=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/06\/aurelie-fontan.jpg\" alt=\"Aur\u00e9lie Fontan\" class=\"wp-image-2945 size-full lazyload\" data-srcset=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/06\/aurelie-fontan.jpg 664w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/06\/aurelie-fontan-199x300.jpg 199w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/06\/aurelie-fontan-133x200.jpg 133w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/06\/aurelie-fontan-83x125.jpg 83w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 664px) 100vw, 664px\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 664px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 664\/1000;\" \/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>A further award for CCAC designer Aurelie Fontan, pioneering development of natural pigments for textile dying.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":2946,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"footnotes":""},"categories":[12],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-2611","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-ccac-news"],"acf":[],"yoast_head":"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v28.5 - https:\/\/yoast.com\/product\/yoast-seo-wordpress\/ -->\n<tit